  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sectoral integrated humanitarian response in DeZ, RD, Aleppo, Idleb - SH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a multisector project (Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), Emergency Food Security and Vulnerable Livelihood (EFSVL), and Protection in all the hubs in Syria. DeZ, Rural Damascus, Aleppo, Idleb. This 12 -month Action aims to address acute humanitarian needs and promote early recovery for vulnerable crisis -affected communities. Beneficiary selection will be conducted through a participatory, inclusive process, ensuring that the most vulnerable are reached. The Action delivers an integrated, flexible, and accountable response in line with Directorate -General for European Civil Protection and Humanitarian Aid Operations (DG ECHO) and Humanitarian Implementation Plans (HIP) 2025 priorities, strengthening the nexus between emergency assistance and early recovery. Under Result 1, WASH interventions include repairing critical water and sewage infrastructures, promoting hygiene behaviour, and rehabilitating WASH facilities in schools. Under Result 2, emergency Multi -Purpose Cash Transfer (MPCT) will support vulnerable households with 6 instalments to cover basic needs. This assistance is expected to improve food consumption and reduce negative coping strategies, while also contributing to national coordination by supporting the Cash Working Group (CWG) through the co -chair role. Under Result 3, Oxfam will rehabilitate two bakeries to increase the availability and access to bread, addressing food insecurity. This intervention aligns with the objective of improving communities&apos; resilience and livelihoods.  The total Beneficiaries (BFs) are Total 218,590 (Female 118,738, Male 99,852)  The locations are as follows: Deir Ez -Zor (DeZ): Al Mayadin, Mahkan, Qorieah, Ashara, Sbeikhan, Tishrine, Dweir, Gharibeh, Dablan, Muhasan, Hatla, Deir Ez -Zor Aleppo: Arada, Barqum, Berna, Hmeira, Kafr Joum Sharki, Zarbah, Zeitan Idleb: Sanjar, Ma&apos;arrat al -Numan Rural Damascus: Mqeilibeh, Artuz, Dhameer, Kisweh The total fund is 5.937.613 (4,250,000 &#x20ac; contribution from European Co</narrative>
  </description>
